WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:35.980
The fate of the Tsukikage Acting Troupe is about to be decided...

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.800
at the District Preliminaries for the Japanese National Acting Competition.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.610
What's more, Hajime Onodera, the manager of the Ondine Troupe,

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.090
has chosen to perform the same piece as them: <i>Takekurabe</i>.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:51.170
Acting prodigy Ayumi Himekawa has been cast in the lead role.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:58.250
Who could know of the dazzling fire that burns deep within the chest of this young girl,

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.080
Maya Kitajima?

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.080
Episode 10 - The Two Midoris of <i>Takekurabe</i>

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.670
What's the deal with the program on the final day?

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.360
I can only imagine it's some crazy coincidence that they've been put on the same day.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:31.230
There's no way the Tsukikage Acting Troupe can win anyway.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.090
I mean, the lead role is being played by...

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:47.300
I'm so happy I get to play the same role as you.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.680
I'm expecting great things from you.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.420
Thank you, Ayumi!

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.240
Can't you tell when someone's being sarcastic?

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:04.980
What?

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.930
Why's she always smiling?

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.380
It's like she doesn't feel threatened by me at all.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.830
Sakurakouji!

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.330
Good luck.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:40.850
Sakurakouji... I thought he'd forgotten all about me.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.120
Daito Troupe

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.790
What are you trying to say, Masumi?

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:48.280
I'm just saying that Tsukikage and Ondine should go head-to-head in a fair fight...

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:53.560
no cheap tricks like putting the Tsukikage Acting Troupe on right after Ondine.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:59.300
If Tsukikage's troupe loses to us, it will merely reflect our superiority over them!

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.790
What? Even though they haven't even been allowed to rehearse on the stage?

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:08.940
Since when did <i>you</i> become the Tsukikage Troupe's knight in shining armor?

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:19.350
This space has the same dimensions as the stage.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.630
Since we've been denied use of the stage,

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.340
let's rehearse by pretending this is the actual stage.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.680
Yeah!

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.870
A purple rose!

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.220
He's here!

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.300
The person who gave me the purple rose... He's here!

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.810
And now, Maya Kitajima, you'll see...

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:24.130
just how hard it is to play a role when you're performing against me!

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.280
You'll find out, plain as day.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.650
You do realize that this is your last chance, don't you?

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.300
If you don't make it through this tournament,

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.190
the Tsukikage Acting Troupe is finished.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.360
You fully understand that, don't you, Ms. Tsukikage?

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:48.370
If you do not make it into the top three after this round,

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.960
you will find yourself with debt so high,

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.330
two lifetimes won't be enough to pay it off.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.190
I'm filled with such happiness.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.460
Here. Recompense for the brushes.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:06.340
Shin!

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:15.510
Why is he always so distant to me when he's not like that with others?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:23.420
He always acts like that to me. In fact, he's never even offered me an adequate reply.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:26.010
He always maintains his distance.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.510
Why is it only me?

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.110
Where are you hiding, Shouta?

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.720
Your presence besmirches this town...

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.230
and you will not escape today!

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.010
Hold!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.190
How does this concern San in the slightest?!

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:50.270
If you wish to brawl with Shouta, then brawl with him!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.930
For what reason are you attacking San?

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.620
Look! Do you see Shouta anywhere?!

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.930
San never ran! He never hid Shouta!

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.670
Stop, Midori!

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.220
Take your hands off me!

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.540
Choukichi, you disgust me!

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.850
If you want to hit someone, then hit me!

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.600
I'll face you!

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.210
She's so intense!

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:18.610
You'd never expect this kind of intensity from Ayumi when she's normally so refined.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:25.180
What gives you the right to talk like that?

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:27.160
You think you are so high and mighty?

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:30.070
Then, this will suit you just fine!

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.510
That's what you deserve.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.510
We have Shinyo as our ally, so any time you wish to return...

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:41.140
we shall be waiting here for you!

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:44.150
Shinyo? You mean, Shin?

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:52.230
So, that was his secret... that was why he refused to look me in the eye.

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.830
What a coward!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.100
Shinyo acts well-mannered in front of everyone,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:00.090
but in actuality, he has been pulling the strings behind the scenes!

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:07.830
He may be a worthy scholar and the heir to the temple...

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.550
but he refuses to take responsibility for his actions.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:17.410
I, Midori of the Daikokuya house, should certainly not be treated in this manner!

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.460
Hey, great job!

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.980
A truly spectacular Midori.

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:27.640
Starting tomorrow, I refuse to attend school!

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:34.030
I refuse! I refuse! I do not even want to <i>see</i> the faces of those cowards!

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:37.640
I do not!

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:59.560
You can't deny how great her acting is.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.790
How could you do something so unseemly?

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:16.120
How could you throw a dirty sandal in her direction?!

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.240
We realize we should not have thrown it, Shin!

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.480
Please don't chase us out!

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:27.780
I should not have mentioned your name during the last fight!

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:33.830
So, this is the reason that Midori has been absent from school.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.540
That monk is so outlandish.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.650
I am convinced that he left because he heard that we were here...

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:46.240
while he was eavesdropping.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.570
It is a shame he left.

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:53.290
If he had walked in, I would have gladly showed him what for!

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:58.470
Hand me some sandals. I will check outside.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.220
Darn. My laces had to come off right here, didn't they?

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:49.170
This is the most telling part of the play.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:28.090
Farewell, young master.

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:29.620
Farewell and take care.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.510
Forget me not, even when you reside in Kyoto.

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:35.900
Farewell, Shin! Farewell!

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:41.090
Let's go, Rei. We're up next.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.560
This little acting competition has become quite interesting!

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:00.990
Wouldn't you agree, Ms. Tsukikage?

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.080
"This little competition," you say?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:09.800
But you're scared, aren't you, Mr. Onodera?

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:17.220
How can Tsukikage even try to perform the same play?

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:18.060
Let's go watch!

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:20.410
Go on ahead.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:22.060
I'll be along later.

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:31.470
Maya's really nervous, isn't she?

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.720
She'll be fine.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.970
Before she gets on stage, she's just like any other girl.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:13:04.890
I'm putting on her mask... Midori's mask.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.450
Why has it gone so quiet?

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:24.020
But everyone cannot help but laugh at San's tomfoolery!

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:26.950
He is so comical!

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:32.550
Oh... are these daffodils?

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.740
When spring arrives, they bloom all over these fields, do they not?

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.180
I adore daffodils.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:45.000
Shin, promise me you'll bring me the most beautiful daffodil when spring arrives!

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:49.420
It must be the prettiest one, promise?

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.660
Indeed. I promise.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:54.970
Oh, I'm filled with such happiness!

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:57.420
Here. Recompense for the brushes.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.420
Shin! Shin!

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:06.800
Why is he always so distant to me when he's not like that with others?

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:16.710
He never acts that way with others... only me.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:23.630
Only... me.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:35.400
What is this sadness? No, it feels more like loneliness...

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:39.190
Ayumi Himekawa presented us with the allure of a woman...

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:42.050
But this is the love of a young girl.

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:43.050
What?

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:46.050
Doesn't this Midori feel kinda new to you?

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.080
Hold!

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.100
I said hold!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.640
How does this concern San in the slightest?!

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:56.100
If you wish to brawl with Shouta, then brawl with him!

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:59.940
Look! Do you see Shouta anywhere?!

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.490
San never ran! He never hid Shouta!

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:03.900
For what reason are you attacking San?

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.520
If you want to hit someone, then hit me!

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.900
I'll face you!

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:13.030
What gives you the right to talk like that?

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:14.960
You think you are so high and mighty?

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:18.100
Then, this will suit you just fine!

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:42.140
Choukichi's behavior disgusts me...

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:45.000
but to be spoken to in such a way is absolutely unacceptable!

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:47.710
Midori...

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:56.790
She's smiling... In a scene where I cried, she's actually smiling!

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:00.690
We will be unable to fight in the future, because Choukichi's right-hand man...

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.820
is going away.

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:06.760
Shin is leaving for a temple in Kyoto, is he not?

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:12.490
The years pass, we grow older and follow different paths...

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.820
I suppose this is the direction life travels in.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.610
What is it, Midori?

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:31.100
Someone has left daffodils here...

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:37.100
Forget me not, even when you reside in Kyoto.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.030
Take care!

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:42.160
Farewell, Shin! Farewell!

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.380
What? What's going on?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.820
Hurry! Bring the TV cameras!

00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:00.270
They've brought the house down!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:18.850
Wow! Our applause is almost as huge as the applause for Ondine was!

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.300
How has this happened?

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:32.270
I was really surprised by that girl!

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:36.840
Yeah, but Ayumi's Midori was truer to the original Midori.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.750
I will now announce the winning troupe!

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.600
The winning troupe is...

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:58.610
the Ondine Troupe, performing <i>Takekurabe<i>!</i></i>

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:15.250
And the Tsukikage Acting Troupe too!

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:19.250
Because both troupes received the same number of points, we have decided that...

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:22.230
these two troupes shall share the honors!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:30.560
They will now have the chance to compete in the National Finals.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:34.010
I'll be going up against her again in the Nationals.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:35.880
Ayumi...

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.550
Sakurakouji!

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:51.690
Let's do our best, Maya.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.620
What are you staring at, Maya?

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:55.640
Everyone's looking at you!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:04.980
Um... Thank you!

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.420
No! My wig!

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:14.100
Let's get out of here.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.060
How embarrassing!

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:19.580
What a clumsy girl! They're all laughing at her!

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:22.070
Yes, she's really something.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:26.250
She knows how to get everyone to look at her.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:31.050
She knows exactly what the audience wants.

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:34.140
Ayumi, it was an accident!

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:35.070
You're right.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:39.060
Because she hasn't realized she's doing it yet.

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:44.590
But if you'd taken a bow, nothing like that would have happened.

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:49.130
How can a girl who's only been acting for a year...

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:52.390
already match me?

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:57.310
I realize now that I haven't given their group the credit they deserved. I underestimated them.

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:59.550
But that won't happen in the Nationals.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.280
I'll make sure of it.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:04.090
Well, this is really something.

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:07.200
I congratulate you on your success.

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:12.000
Ms. Tsukikage. Everyone...

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.370
I have to admit, I didn't envision you making it this far.

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:20.370
Yes, I apologize, but it looks like we exceeded your expectations...

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:21.870
and took first place after all.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:24.640
Oh my, that stings.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:30.280
But my expectations are unchanged for the National Competition.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.690
Right, everyone. Go on ahead.

00:20:35.550 --> 00:20:37.130
Oh, it's you!

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.910
Your Midori was pretty good, you know.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:41.850
Groundbreaking, even.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:53.930
I've never seen such a tomboyish Midori.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.340
No, I meant it. I really liked it!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:03.550
Masumi Hayami is not to be underestimated.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:09.170
What's this?

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:11.000
It says it's for Maya Kitajima!

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:14.920
Congratulations!

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.350
The Nationals are next.

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:19.260
I wish you luck.

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:24.460
It's filled with chocolates!

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:25.920
They look so good!

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:30.040
Thank you, Mr. or Mrs. Flowers!

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:33.970
Please come watch us in the Nationals!

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:39.710
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe have finally secured their place in the National Competition.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:46.410
Maya's heart is overflowing with hope, but she has no way of knowing...

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:49.060
that there are many tests for her to pass before she can reach that point.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:25.490
It looks like you've finally made it to the National Competition, little one.

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:28.080
Your rival, Ayumi Himekawa, has been honing her skills as well,

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:30.740
and has improved greatly since the preliminaries.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:35.720
And there's a new rival troupe from Hokkaido with a unique sense of humor.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:40.900
I'm really looking forward to seeing what kind of act you'll entertain us with on the big stage!

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:45.490
You have no props, nor costumes... and even your friends have disappeared.

00:23:46.310 --> 00:23:49.800
Will the Tsukikage Acting Troupe be able to continue?

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:51.500
